# File: tests/features/add_greeting_hex_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/212-add-greeting-hex-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Encode the completed greeting as lowercase hexadecimal text

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Return the hex text of the completed greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_hex is called with Ada
    Then the result is the Python str 48656c6c6f2c20416461
    And it is 20 characters long, two per UTF-8 byte of Hello, Ada

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Encode exact UTF-8 code points as lowercase hex without separators
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_hex is called with Zo followed by precomposed U+00EB, with Zoe followed by combining U+0308, and with U+00E9 followed by U+4E2D
    Then the results are 48656c6c6f2c205a6fc3ab, 48656c6c6f2c205a6f65cc88, and 48656c6c6f2c20c3a9e4b8ad
    And every result contains only the characters 0-9 and a-f with no separators

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_hex is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing existing surfaces
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_hex of Ada, and nmg-smoke Ada runs
    Then the example prints 48656c6c6f2c20416461
    And greeting_hex is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__ alongside every previously listed export
    And nmg-smoke prints Hello, Ada with one newline and exit status 0
    And the README documents UTF-8 encoding of the complete greeting, the lowercase two-characters-per-byte format without separators or prefix, the absence of Unicode normalization, and the inherited invalid-name error
